Package: ratiod
Title: Bayesian Hierarchical Models for Ratios, Rates, and Proportions
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: An opinionated framework for Bayesian hierarchical modelling of
    ratios, rates, and proportions. Ratios are treated as derived quantities,
    with all inference performed on the latent processes generating the numerator
    and denominator. Supports shared random effects, latent factors for unmeasured
    confounders, spatial structure ('CAR'/'BYM2'/'GP'), and full uncertainty
    propagation to ratio posteriors. Provides multiple inference backends
    including custom 'HMC'/'NUTS' (default), 'Laplace' approximation,
    and 'Polya-Gamma' Gibbs sampling.
